! REPRODUCER, a MODEL finding (docs/NEXT.md, "G2.1 CHAPTER 4: LOCATION 8
! AS A FLOATING-POINT OPERAND", second part: the STORE).
!
! Reference Manual printed p.96 (PDF 99), Store Rounded (SRD): "The
! rounding is performed by adding one to the fraction in the accumulator
! in bit position 60 ... The 48 low-order bits are discarded ... The
! sign of the accumulator, as changed by the sign modifiers, is placed
! in storage bit 60.  The accumulator flag bits are placed in storage
! bits 61-63.  The entire accumulator and its sign byte register remain
! unchanged throughout the operation unless used as the effective
! address."
!
! CHANGED 2026-11-16: THE STORE IS NOW "SRDN(N), $L".  The printed form
! "SRDN, $L", with no dds, is not a floating-point instruction at all:
! both assemblers compile it as the VFL STORE ROUNDED, code 101101 (C22-6578
! printed p.30, Problem 3.5 comment (c): "An operation which could be
! either VFL or floating-point is assumed VFL"), which the model does not
! implement -- it turns OP on, and the trace said so ("OP site =
! vflIntOp/unimplemented-code code=101101").  THAT was the "lost store"
! below; the floating-point store to 8 had a fault of its own all the
! same (it wrote word 8 whole, sign into bit 60).
!
! WHAT p.80 SAYS THE STORE DOES, settled 2026-11-16 in the ink (printed
! p.80, PDF 83): "The four sign byte bits replace the four low-order bits
! of the accumulator operand.  Bits 60-63 of the accumulator do not serve
! as operand bits.  For all floating-point single-precision operations,
! they remain unchanged. ... This rule applies to operations of both
! fetch and store type."  So the stored word's bits 0-59 go to
! accumulator 0-59, its bits 60-63 (sign, flags) to $SB bits 4-7, and
! accumulator bits 60-63 keep their 1110.  The "003B 851E B851 EB78" below
! read word 8 as an ordinary word; p.80's answer is
!   word 8   003B 851E B851 EB7E    (rounded 0-59, bits 60-63 unchanged)
!   word 9   147A E147 AE20 0000    (untouched)
!   word 10  0800 0000 0000 0000    ($SB: minus from N, flags 000)
! Registered with those three checks; PC 67, and all pass (bsv/
! StretchExecute.bsv fpStoreToLoc8).

! INJECTION 2, measured 2026-11-16 (fpStoreToLoc8 disabled, so word 8 is
! written whole, the old store), over the same 28 lines: FAILED the store
! repro's W8 (003B851EB851EB78) and $SB (0); problem_3_fp_address_8_sign's
! R4 (+5, 006A000000000000), word 8 (006A000000000008) and $SB (0).
! Nothing else -- in particular 4.12/4.13's "SRT(N), $L" and Problem 3.3
! Method 3's "SRD(N), 8.0" pass either way, so they do not witness this.
!
! THE ORIGINAL RECORD, 2026-11-16, of the VFL form:
!
! Here the effective address IS location 8.  The accumulator holds
! s*s, s = .6 as assembled (0009 9999 9999 9990), double length.  Its
! bits 60-63 are fraction bits 49-52 of s*s = 1110, so ROUNDING CARRIES
! INTO BIT 59: the stored fraction is B851E B851 EB7, the unrounded one
! ...EB6.  Worked by hand from p.96, "SRDN, $L" must leave in word 8
!   exponent -1, fraction rounded, sign 1 (N inverts plus), flags 000:
!   003B 851E B851 EB78
! and whatever p.96's "unless used as the effective address" does to
! $SB, bits 0-59 of word 8 must end ...EB7.
!
! THE MODEL, OBSERVED 2026-11-16 with words 8-10 dumped:
!   word 8   003B 851E B851 EB6E   bits 0-59 UNROUNDED, bits 60-63 the
!                                  accumulator's own fraction bits
!   word 10  0000 0000 0000 0000   $SB unchanged, still plus
! So the store did not happen at all, by either reading of p.96: it is
! not a sign byte routed to $SB instead of word 8.  (An earlier version
! of this deck used t*t, t = 1/3, whose rounding does not carry; it
! could not tell a lost store from a redirected sign byte.)
!
! Registered pinned at the model's WRONG words; flip both when fixed.
! SRT(N), $L (4.12, 4.13) DOES take effect in the model; this is SRD's.
!
! Found by C22-6578 Problem 4.9, printed p.43, "SRDN,$L", the last
! store of COSF (decks/problem_4_9_method1.strap).

START   DL(N), SIX
        D*(N), SIX
        SRDN(N), $L
HALT    BEW, $
SIX     DD(N), .6
        END, START
